{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012DkNrv7YX3vvRkvT9f3MTZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018s4HjY4TUfEjgcWT2T6uRX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-1200-bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers\n\nReplace per-matrix GPU buffer allocation in MLE sumcheck fold rounds with bulk pre-allocated arena buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~2000 individual DeviceBuffers for fold output matrices (one per trace matrix for both mat_evals and sels), totaling ~40K cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync calls across ~20 rounds. This per-round allocation overhead causes MLE Rounds to reverse-scale at APC 300 (173ms vs 114ms at APC 0 despite 2x less work), contributing ~59ms of pure CUDA memory API overhead on the main thread. By allocating a single contiguous buffer per fold group per round, we reduce 40K allocations to ~40, eliminating the per-matrix allocation/free overhead and improving memory pool behavior for subsequent phases.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1863,"cache_read_input_tokens":142557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1863},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8941d98-8943-40ba-ba2b-e8ee56c821e0","uuid":"1058ec43-938e-496f-9f33-d9e1b5710c1d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018s4HjY4TUfEjgcWT2T6uRX","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8941d98-8943-40ba-ba2b-e8ee56c821e0","uuid":"59e0bdad-63d1-4f7a-b024-50a411cec2e8","timestamp":"2026-04-14T10:12:41.658Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-1200-bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers\n\nReplace per-matrix GPU buffer allocation in MLE sumcheck fold rounds with bulk pre-allocated arena buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~2000 individual DeviceBuffers for fold output matrices (one per trace matrix for both mat_evals and sels), totaling ~40K cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync calls across ~20 rounds. This per-round allocation overhead causes MLE Rounds to reverse-scale at APC 300 (173ms vs 114ms at APC 0 despite 2x less work), contributing ~59ms of pure CUDA memory API overhead on the main thread. By allocating a single contiguous buffer per fold group per round, we reduce 40K allocations to ~40, eliminating the per-matrix allocation/free overhead and improving memory pool behavior for subsequent phases.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval","+# 2026-04-14-1200-bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers"," ","-Batch SCATTER-mode GKR input evaluation AIRs into a single descriptor-array CUDA kernel launch per segment, running on a dedicated background thread concurrent with the existing multi-stream GLOBAL-mode processing. At APC 300, ~305 of the 791 GKR input eval kernel instances use SCATTER mode (buffer_size <= 10), each launching a tiny kernel (median 111us, 4-16 blocks). These underutilize the GPU's 128 SMs when launched individually. By consolidating all SCATTER AIRs into one batched kernel (following the established `batch_mle` descriptor-array pattern), we eliminate ~305 kernel launches and their CPU-side overhead, while freeing the 8 multi-stream worker threads to focus exclusively on the ~486 compute-heavy GLOBAL-mode AIRs. The SCATTER batch runs concurrently on a separate thread, completely hidden behind the GLOBAL processing.","+Replace per-matrix GPU buffer allocation in MLE sumcheck fold rounds with bulk pre-allocated arena buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~2000 individual DeviceBuffers for fold output matrices (one per trace matrix for both mat_evals and sels), totaling ~40K cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync calls across ~20 rounds. This per-round allocation overhead causes MLE Rounds to reverse-scale at APC 300 (173ms vs 114ms at APC 0 despite 2x less work), contributing ~59ms of pure CUDA memory API overhead on the main thread. By allocating a single contiguous buffer per fold group per round, we reduce 40K allocations to ~40, eliminating the per-matrix allocation/free overhead and improving memory pool behavior for subsequent phases."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval\n\nBatch SCATTER-mode GKR input evaluation AIRs into a single descriptor-array CUDA kernel launch per segment, running on a dedicated background thread concurrent with the existing multi-stream GLOBAL-mode processing. At APC 300, ~305 of the 791 GKR input eval kernel instances use SCATTER mode (buffer_size <= 10), each launching a tiny kernel (median 111us, 4-16 blocks). These underutilize the GPU's 128 SMs when launched individually. By consolidating all SCATTER AIRs into one batched kernel (following the established `batch_mle` descriptor-array pattern), we eliminate ~305 kernel launches and their CPU-side overhead, while freeing the 8 multi-stream worker threads to focus exclusively on the ~486 compute-heavy GLOBAL-mode AIRs. The SCATTER batch runs concurrently on a separate thread, completely hidden behind the GLOBAL processing.\n"}}
