{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SGNebDC5FVGZCYLw2dKncM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-1200-bulk-alloc-mle-fold-buffers\n2\t\n3\tReplace per-matrix GPU buffer allocation in MLE sumcheck fold rounds with bulk pre-allocated arena buffers. Currently, each MLE round allocates ~2000 individual DeviceBuffers for fold output matrices (one per trace matrix for both mat_evals and sels), totaling ~40K cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync calls across ~20 rounds. This per-round allocation overhead causes MLE Rounds to reverse-scale at APC 300 (173ms vs 114ms at APC 0 despite 2x less work), contributing ~59ms of pure CUDA memory API overhead on the main thread. By allocating a single contiguous buffer per fold group per round, we reduce 40K allocations to ~40, eliminating the per-matrix allocation/free overhead and improving memory pool behavior for subsequent phases.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01V3aPTUM9QJQz1Ej31gwMjm","session_id":"a8941d98-8943-40ba-ba2b-e8ee56c821e0","uuid":"96bc2fd9-aa6b-4df9-b752-00a8380ad51a","timestamp":"2026-04-14T10:16:23.787Z"}
